    description: ""  # afae
    fields:  # afae
      statement: "Pressing Ctrl-C during 'hypergumbo run' produces a raw Python KeyboardInterrupt traceback (with concurrent.futures internals) rather than a graceful 'Aborted by user' message. Exit code is correctly 130. No partial output file is created (good). The traceback creates noise and looks like a crash even though the behavior is intentional."  # afae
      root_cause: "ThreadPoolExecutor's as_completed() blocks in a wait() loop; SIGINT bubbles up as KeyboardInterrupt with no top-level handler."  # afae
